
# 🏦 FinSight: Automated Loan Approval Prediction System

[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.12-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/)
[![Jupyter](https://img.shields.io/badge/Jupyter-Notebook-orange.svg)](https://jupyter.org/)
[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green.svg)](LICENSE)

An end-to-end machine learning project that predicts loan approval decisions with **93.75% accuracy**, demonstrating how AI can automate financial underwriting processes.

---

## 📊 Project Overview

FinSight is a machine learning system that analyzes credit bureau data and applicant information to predict loan approval decisions. This project showcases the complete data science workflow from data exploration to model deployment preparation.

**Key Highlights:**
- 🎯 **93.75% Accuracy** with 0.99 AUC score
- 🔍 **12 ML Algorithms** tested and compared systematically
- 📈 **Robust Validation** using cross-validation (92.99% ± 0.08%)
- 💡 **Feature Analysis** identifying debt-to-income ratio as top predictor
- 🛠️ **Production-Ready** model persistence and preprocessing pipeline

---

## 🎯 Problem Statement

Financial institutions manually review thousands of loan applications, with each taking 2-3 days and costing $50-100 in labor. This project explores how machine learning can automate this process while maintaining high accuracy and consistency.

**Challenge:** Build a binary classification model that predicts loan approval/rejection based on applicant financial and demographic data.

